s first match as Germany coach. The former Liverpool and Borussia Dortmund boss has big ambitions, but the game showed he's going to need more time to achieve them.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>UNGA Day 3: Netanyahu defends Israel as delegates walk out</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:690c4ee7aeac6543fda1e279a792f8fd5acaaaa9f6155b1d78fa581e511c2ab1</id><updated>2026-09-25T05:07:58Z</updated><published>2026-09-24T19:11:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/unga-day-3-netanyahu-defends-israel-as-delegates-walk-out/live-79366211--ad1d3eff9b7d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/unga-day-3-netanyahu-defends-israel-as-delegates-walk-out/live-79366211?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu called accusing Israel of genocide in Gaza the "greatest lie of the century." Many delegates walked out for his General Assembly speech. Mahmoud Abbas also spoke via video.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Three-way battle for power in world chess: Who will be elected FIDE president in Samarkand?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:440679a12d1f2f49a3f404a9d657ce332bf9fa391717016c8df370dd53e1455e</id><updated>2026-09-25T05:06:54Z</updated><published>2026-09-24T18:59:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/three-way-battle-for-power-in-world-chess-who-will-be-elected-fide-president-in-samarkand/a-79413301--bc60333e85fc.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/three-way-battle-for-power-in-world-chess-who-will-be-elected-fide-president-in-samarkand/a-79413301?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The era of Russian presidents is coming to an end at the World Chess Federation (FIDE). Two Germans and one Kazakh are up for election. Among the issues at play are money, Kremlin influence, and unanswered questions.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Ethiopia's military says it killed hundreds of TPLF rebels</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b0d6652bba73b0166fad7908173a5e9e6ca14c983159998ac9c077a995323cf0</id><updated>2026-09-25T05:06:54Z</updated><published>2026-09-24T18:37:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/ethiopia-s-military-says-it-killed-hundreds-of-tplf-rebels/a-79419173--d10c751c44c1.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/ethiopia-s-military-says-it-killed-hundreds-of-tplf-rebels/a-79419173?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The TPLF fought against against the Ethiopian military from 2020 to 2022 in a conflict that saw hundreds of thousands of civilians killed. A resumption of fighting has sparked fears of another brutal war.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>After several difficult years, economists now expect German economy to grow</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f1e5e60ae31e6b290f8fbc3af3272fefe977f8cfa4a52615ca17eeb61856b806</id><updated>2026-09-25T05:06:54Z</updated><published>2026-09-24T17:04:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/after-several-difficult-years-economists-now-expect-german-economy-to-grow/a-79418591--9a99d252976e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/after-several-difficult-years-economists-now-expect-german-economy-to-grow/a-79418591?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Germany's economy is growing again, but recovery remains on shaky ground. High government spending is keeping the economy afloat, while energy prices, a shortage of skilled workers and debt continue to weigh on it.</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>CNN, MS NOW, Politico regain access to White House</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9ff0696af47a1728f45876ebb1331764a8b9caaca1b70c4beb42fdb601a1bcbe</id><updated>2026-09-25T05:06:54Z</updated><published>2026-09-24T16:41:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/cnn-ms-now-politico-regain-access-to-white-house/a-79405693--d2a4fb75d5c1.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/cnn-ms-now-politico-regain-access-to-white-house/a-79405693?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A federal judge has ordered President Trump to restore White House access to CNN, MS NOW and Politico after he banned the media outlets from the premises. Hours later, the media announced they had been granted access.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Houthi advances in Yemen drive displacement, deepen humanitarian crisis</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ca918543911f30a6325f39c5f756308a1db33ccd88bc3c825aa587c7af8ac946</id><updated>2026-09-25T05:06:54Z</updated><published>2026-09-24T16:26:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/houthi-advances-in-yemen-drive-displacement-deepen-humanitarian-crisis/a-79414280--b87656e50311.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/houthi-advances-in-yemen-drive-displacement-deepen-humanitarian-crisis/a-79414280?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">With more than 132,000 people already displaced by the latest fighting and Houthi territorial gains, Yemen is on the brink of slipping back into a full-fledged humanitarian emergency. DW spoke with people on the ground.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Nigeria, US agree to boost mining investment on sidelines of UN General Assembly</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8cc561e060ed75e0b32110799e902a81f9b62eaee86739d8e109de378676c8fa</id><updated>2026-09-25T05:06:54Z</updated><published>2026-09-24T15:46:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/nigeria-us-agree-to-boost-mining-investment-on-sidelines-of-un-general-assembly/a-79417444--0b49b11ac5c8.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/nigeria-us-agree-to-boost-mining-investment-on-sidelines-of-un-general-assembly/a-79417444?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">On the sidelines of the UN General Assembly, Nigeria and the US inked a new mining deal. Nigeria is home to deposits of lithium, gold, tin, gemstones, iron ore and phosphate.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Extremist parties are thriving ― and that scares people</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:99f95addee7862426502037683233537d6a52d371df52d6b0f91d78c181045bf</id><updated>2026-09-25T05:06:54Z</updated><published>2026-09-24T14:00:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/extremist-parties-are-thriving-_-and-that-scares-people/a-79410960--03e11a3885b2.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/extremist-parties-are-thriving-―-and-that-scares-people/a-79410960?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Far-right and far-left parties are celebrating success after success, leaving moderate politicians in the dust and worrying many Germans. Political psychology helps us understand what's behind growing polarization.</summary><category term="Science" /></entry><entry><title>How renewed fighting in Tigray could spread across the Horn of Africa</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:59f9b3ef8dfa9b6be887f76ccaa29915fdbb3df29eb2895c73d3a451aba240ef</id><updated>2026-09-25T05:06:54Z</updated><published>2026-09-24T13:59:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/how-renewed-fighting-in-tigray-could-spread-across-the-horn-of-africa/a-79410333--a598375bf2c9.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/how-renewed-fighting-in-tigray-could-spread-across-the-horn-of-africa/a-79410333?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The fresh hostilities in Ethiopia's Tigray region come after months of growing animosity between rebel forces and the federal government. Horn of Africa expert Martin Plaut warns of possible regional spillover.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Donald Trump hosts Xi Jinping for state dinner with tech titans. Follow live.</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d2b47ae4078f192212894166d13f3818aa05355c7f4c3886c04da72a60d416c2</id><updated>2026-09-25T05:08:01Z</updated><published>2026-09-24T13:37:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/donald-trump-hosts-xi-jinping-for-state-dinner-with-tech-titans-follow-live/live-79404511--d8b5960a2742.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/donald-trump-hosts-xi-jinping-for-state-dinner-with-tech-titans-follow-live/live-79404511?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Donald Trump rolled out the red carpet for Chinese leader Xi Jinping, with the two having toasted each other at a lavish state dinner after their summit meeting. America's top tech bosses were also present at the dinner.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>EU to condemn war in Ukraine at G20 even if Putin attends</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:836d0d6ecb97299844742ddcaf8dd46a79c3d97bcae0d857d890b7c0f46a00e0</id><updated>2026-09-25T05:06:54Z</updated><published>2026-09-24T13:30:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/eu-to-condemn-war-in-ukraine-at-g20-even-if-putin-attends/a-79413317--3809a660b511.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/eu-to-condemn-war-in-ukraine-at-g20-even-if-putin-attends/a-79413317?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Russian President Vladimir Putin has been invited to the G20 summit in Miami by the United States. Multiple members of the group have called for Moscow's exclusion over its invasion of Ukraine.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>AI systems shifted their answers toward both left- and right-leaning users in a study. Could sycophantic chatbots deepen political divides?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:fe27750d4941d2556238a1801184a49e0cfd8e6648d2ecdb90b5748182a71e5e</id><updated>2026-09-25T05:06:54Z</updated><published>2026-09-24T13:10:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/ai-systems-shifted-their-answers-toward-both-left-and-right-leaning-users-in-a-study-could-sycophant/a-79377894--6126140be276.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/ai-systems-shifted-their-answers-toward-both-left-and-right-leaning-users-in-a-study-could-sycophantic-chatbots-deepen-political-divides/a-79377894?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A study shows chatbots mirror users' politics, part of a broader tendency known as AI sycophancy. Researchers fear this could deepen polarization.</summary><category term="Science" /></entry><entry><title>Germany news: Berlin officially withdraws Olympics bid</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8749fa8f47b0fbdaa2bf7f335e7bf79f6c81f21752eff03b24334f1567339a0b</id><updated>2026-09-25T05:06:54Z</updated><published>2026-09-24T12:42:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-news-berlin-officially-withdraws-olympics-bid/live-79406294--30622a12ce08.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-news-berlin-officially-withdraws-olympics-bid/live-79406294?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Berlin's decision to withdraw its Olympic bid means that only Munich and the western Rhine/Ruhr region are left in the running as potential Olympic hosts. DW has more.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Czech PM Andrej Babis reiterates importance of NATO for his country but rejects calls to increase defense spending</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:29ae087b1e3e154a23ccecc1f26811b05a29256796006b87512507b61f016046</id><updated>2026-09-25T05:06:54Z</updated><published>2026-09-24T12:11:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/czech-pm-andrej-babis-reiterates-importance-of-nato-for-his-country-but-rejects-calls-to-increase-de/a-79411066--415ccd460a40.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/czech-pm-andrej-babis-reiterates-importance-of-nato-for-his-country-but-rejects-calls-to-increase-defense-spending/a-79411066?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The US and NATO want Czechia to spend more on defense. Czech Prime Minister Andrej Babis says Prague cannot afford faster increases, despite growing warnings about the threat from Russia.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>'Pope fever' takes hold as Pope Leo visits France</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:1f7da3b3e48e27d7ed141840736d0716edaa8924b14f34a3bbd519e2a9027c80</id><updated>2026-09-25T05:06:54Z</updated><published>2026-09-24T12:03:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/pope-fever-takes-hold-as-pope-leo-visits-france/a-79401291--1edb64ca4ad9.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/pope-fever-takes-hold-as-pope-leo-visits-france/a-79401291?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Pope Leo XIV is expected to draw huge crowds during his visit to France. As part of his trip, he's also set to address Europe's future and some of the challenges ahead.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>EU finally clinching trade deals with Southeast Asian states</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5ea147652c5f4394c9255ca12d5c6530c18a10396eaa4e744c211570a8680054</id><updated>2026-09-25T05:06:54Z</updated><published>2026-09-24T11:40:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/eu-finally-clinching-trade-deals-with-southeast-asian-states/a-79388278--8c0030248950.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/eu-finally-clinching-trade-deals-with-southeast-asian-states/a-79388278?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">After years of arduous negotiations, the EU is closing on a string of bilateral trade deals with countries in Southeast Asia. And yet, a bloc-to-bloc agreement between the EU and ASEAN remains a distant prospect.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Tensions between India and Bangladesh are in focus after Dhaka skipped the BRICS summit in Delhi</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ae9cdf9bfb2f49ee41cac7d1e9033a68c803b217921735615d17e07ffa151eed</id><updated>2026-09-25T05:06:54Z</updated><published>2026-09-24T11:37:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/tensions-between-india-and-bangladesh-are-in-focus-after-dhaka-skipped-the-brics-summit-in-delhi/a-79410667--fb62a16b78a2.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/tensions-between-india-and-bangladesh-are-in-focus-after-dhaka-skipped-the-brics-summit-in-delhi/a-79410667?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Bangladesh's absence from the BRICS summit in New Delhi has raised fresh questions about strained ties. Ousted PM Sheikh Hasina's exile in India remains a major obstacle to normalizing relations.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>India news: Cockroach party demands Election Commissioner Gyanesh Kumar's resignation</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2a0b8b73316d09b43a1174c43239317a8209030a9e1a23a1ef13152e9e022a8b</id><updated>2026-09-25T05:06:54Z</updated><published>2026-09-24T11:28:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/india-news-cockroach-party-demands-election-commissioner-gyanesh-kumar-s-resignation/live-79405879--428579042cfb.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/india-news-cockroach-party-demands-election-commissioner-gyanesh-kumar-s-resignation/live-79405879?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">CJP's Abhijeet Dipke has alleged that the removal of more than 130 million names from draft electoral rolls is designed to benefit the BJP and weaken opposition parties. DW has more.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Poland says Starlink station fire 'act of sabotage'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:42b189ee024d5327a25e6319919b1607b64712fdb5a5942cca40f1373c51c711</id><updated>2026-09-25T05:06:54Z</updated><published>2026-09-24T10:21:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/poland-says-starlink-station-fire-act-of-sabotage/a-79410745--549d54958cd1.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/poland-says-starlink-station-fire-act-of-sabotage/a-79410745?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Polish Deputy Prime Minister Krzysztof Gawkowski said Warsaw believed the attack aimed to disrupt internet access for the Ukrainian military, calling it "an element of the next phase of hybrid warfare."</summary><category term="News" /></entry></feed>
